\begin_layout Standard
Q1 :
 The diameter of a wire measured by a screw gauge of least count 0.001 cm is 0.08 cm.
 The length measured by a scale of least count 0.1 cm is 150 cm.
 When a weight of 100 N is applied to the wire,
 the extension in length is 0.5 cm,
 measured by a micrometer of least count 0.001 cm.
 The error in the measurement of Young's Modulus is 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha\times10^{9}\;N/m^{2}$
\end_inset

.
 The value of 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset

 is _________.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
(Ignore the contribution of load to Young's Modulus error calculation)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\lang english
[ JEE Mains 2nd April 2026 Shift 1 ]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A) 1.3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
B) 1.65
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
C) 0.13
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
D) 0.25
\end_layout

